WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.533
The FBI

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.802
is searching President Biden's home

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.105
in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, right now.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.707
This is part of the ongoing investigation

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.110
into his handling of classified documents

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.177
Biden's attorney

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:11.911
put out a statement

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.146
saying that the search

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.914
was planned in advance

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.250
and that the president is cooperating.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.084
Today's search

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:18.885
now makes it

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.954
the third known location

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.689
that federal agents have gone through

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:22.989
to look

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.225
for classified material at the properties

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.360
associated with President Biden.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.328
Paula Reid,

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.596
she's joining us now from Washington.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:30.530
With much more on this.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.265
Paula, this all started really unfolding

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.233
just a little while ago.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.467
What are you learning?

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:34.868
That's right.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.102
Pool cameras actually

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.203
spotted vehicles

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.605
and what appeared to be federal agents

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.873
at the Rehoboth House.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.007
And they were there because, Kate,

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.142
we have very much expected

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.910
that there would likely be an FBI

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.311
search of this property.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:45.979
And as you noted,

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.947
this is being conducted in cooperation

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.482
with the president's attorneys

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.850
But to put this in context

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.352
and explain why we expected this.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.520
Let's go back to the beginning

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.721
of this situation.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.288
They uncovered

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.823
classified documents of the president's

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.892
former office back in November.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.526
Several weeks

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.226
after that,

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.494
the president's own attorneys

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.396
decided out of an abundance of caution

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.531
to search his homes

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.932
in Wilmington, Delaware,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.068
and this property in Rehoboth.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:08.568
And they've said

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.335
that they did find

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.037
classified materials in Wilmington,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.106
but they did not find any in Rehoboth.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.774
And that subsequently became

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.309
the subject of a full blown

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.044
special counsel investigation.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:18.978
And it was expected

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.547
that the FBI would want to go

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.915
and do its own searches.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.916
Roughly two weeks ago,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.283
of course,

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.584
the FBI did its own

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.552
search of the president's

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:26.486
Wilmington home,

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.320
and they uncovered

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.222
additional classified materials.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.323
So we're expecting them

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.525
to show up in Rehoboth eventually.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.393
That is today.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.661
Of course, it's unclear, though,

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.096
how long this search will take.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.230
Kate, the one in Wilmington

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.332
lasted roughly 13 hours.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.433
But the big question

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:40.767
now is

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.701
whether they will find

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.037
any additional classified materials.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:44.971
As of now,

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:45.572
our sources

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.540
say the total classified documents

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.241
that have been found will

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.209
that the former office

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.376
and at the Wilmington home

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.445
its characterized as dozens

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.480
known to date.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.147
A big question,

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.715
will they find additional material?

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:56.583
And if so, will

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.917
they share that information

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:58.685
with the public?

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.553
There's been a real push and pull

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.422
in terms of transparency here.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.523
They confirm this search

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.325
after we caught it on camera.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.026
They have provided some details,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.161
but most of the information

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.362
in this investigation

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.131
has come out through the press.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.232
Yeah, that was

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.566
that was what I was going to ask you is

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.602
is is how quickly it's expected.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.870
If there is something found,

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.638
what will when the public will learn?

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.105
We'll stand by

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.073
to stand by with you on that one.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:20.840
Paula, thank you so much.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.708
I really appreciate it.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.842
Joining me now for more on

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.410
this is CNN legal analyst

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.411
Elliot Williams.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.746
He's a former federal prosecutor.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.214
Elliot, thanks for jumping on.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.383
What do you make of the statement?

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.718
What do you make of this search?

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.519
Also, the statement

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.287
coming out from Biden's attorney

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.221
and it was.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.356
Let me read just part of it,

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:36.723
because it's

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.525
what Paula was talking about.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.361
She said the statement from Bob Barr was,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.163
Under DOJ standard procedures

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.697
in the interest of operational security

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.431
and integrity,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.533
it sought to do this work

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.635
without advance public notice.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.103
And we agreed to cooperate.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:50.703
What do you make of that?

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.072
You know, it's a little confusing

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.175
because it's the Justice Department

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.243
in Joe Biden's administration.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:57.877
That's putting it out.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.546
There are two different entities, right.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.847
You have the Justice Department

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.849
that kind of operates independently.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.617
And then you have the White House.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.418
Now, look,

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.953
they have different interests here.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.087
And the Justice Department's

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.956
key interest is maintaining

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.958
secrecy around its search.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.393
And that's why,

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:13.693
you know,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.862
they did not publicly announce it.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.563
They just didn't

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.331
publicly announce the search and so on.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.267
Right now, why they were able to come

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.268
to some

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.637
consent agreement to search their home,

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:25.939
is that the just

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.240
assume that they wouldn't

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.341
have gotten into a fight

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.976
over the documents with the fight.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.010
But the Biden team.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.644
I think the Justice

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.146
Department operated under the assumption

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.915
that they weren't expecting the president

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.817
or his aides to conceal

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.285
or hide or tamper with evidence.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.721
That's why they came to some agreement

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.722
as to the search here.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.056
But again,

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.490
it can be a little bit confusing

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.425
because, yes,

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.593
it is the Justice Department

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.461
yes, it's an independent entity,

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.462
but it's not the same thing

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.463
as the White House. Right.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.098
Even though it's the same president.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:52.599
And we know

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.399
to this point

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.236
that when Biden's team went through that

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:56.836
the home,

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:57.570
the Rehoboth home,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.304
they said that they

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.372
did not find any

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.773
classified documents there.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.475
If the FBI, through this search,

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.810
does find more documents

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.778
at this home at this point,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:06.980
How problematic is that?

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:09.749
It's problematic

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.083
if the

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.784
FBI uncovers evidence

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.586
that there was intentional

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.588
taking or mishandling of documents

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.190
Look, Kate,

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.859
I had classified a top secret clearance

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.560
for many years.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.995
It can be

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:24.264
easier than you think or hope

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.498
for classified documents.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:25.999
To get out.

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.333
Most of the time

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.901
that it happens, it's inadvertent.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.670
Someone takes a document out

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.071
accidentally or so on.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.273
That may have been the case here.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.341
Now, if the FBI uncovers evidence

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.442
that someone

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.577
and not just the president,

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.545
someone around the president on his team

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.649
voluntarily, knowingly took documents

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.384
away from the White House,

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:45.351
away from the scrutiny

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.753
of the National Records Administration.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.421
Then, of course,

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.322
it should be alarming

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.957
because that can be a federal crime,

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.458
but most of the time

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.461
it simply would be an accident.

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:56.763
Classified documents

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.798
got out of where they should have been.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.566
We also have reporting this morning

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:01.200
from Paul

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.902
Raitt as well that the special counsel,

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:03.569
Robert Hunter,

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:06.372
is now officially on the job.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.508
And he obviously is a special counsel

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.542
who will be overseeing

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.077
this investigation into Biden's

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.812
handling of classified documents

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:15.048
watching from the outside

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:15.481
Elliot,

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.916
is there anything that we're going

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.918
to see that changes

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.420
now that he is running things?

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.523
I really don't think so, and

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.190
I really don't think

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.224
it should be the case.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:25.591
Look, in

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.460
any well-functioning organization,

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.461
not even government

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.762
or the Justice Department

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.098
moving in and out, that the head

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.032
the principle

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.367
ought not to change the work

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:34.967
they were doing.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.769
They were proceeding beforehand

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.871
with investigations and searches and

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.807
and going through evidence

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.209
even prior to Bob, her coming on now,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.211
but having somebody as a

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.246
as a figurehead at the top can help

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.247
steer the ship

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.083
and make sure things are red,

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:52.685
are handled and proceeding effectively.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:53.820
But the direction

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.821
shouldn't really change.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:54.987
I mean,

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.622
I think that would actually be quite bad

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.390
for government.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.125
Every time a new U.S.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.394
attorney or a new special counsel came in

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.263
things fell apart

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.565
or changed quite dramatically.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.166
So I'm not anticipating

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.201
things will be much different.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.502
And look, at a minimum,

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:10.103
you can be certain

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:10.703
that the judge

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:11.938
is not going to start

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:12.372
talking

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.940
about the investigations

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.607
they're doing now

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.142
simply because someone else is coming in.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.643
Their M.O., for better

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.811
or worse, is simply

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:19.879
to just keep their mouth shut.

